[h1]Enshrouded Sleep — Public Beta[/h1]

Proportional multiplayer sleeping for Project Zomboid Build 42 servers.

[b]Version:[/b] 0.1.1
[b]Tested with:[/b] Project Zomboid 42.20.4
[b]Workshop ID:[/b] 3786842301
[b]Mod ID:[/b] pz-enshrouded-sleep

[h2]What it does[/h2]
When some, but not all, living players are asleep, Enshrouded Sleep proportionally compresses world/calendar time while awake players continue moving, fighting, driving, crafting, and interacting at normal active-simulation speed.

Public Beta v0.1.1 protects awake players from the extra survival-needs/metabolism progression caused by that calendar compression. Hunger, thirst, fatigue, calories, carbohydrates, proteins, lipids, and weight progression are normalized toward the rate expected at the server's native day length. Sleeping players are never corrected.

When all living players are asleep, Enshrouded Sleep restores the native day length and vanilla Project Zomboid full-sleep fast-forward takes over.

[h2]What's new in v0.1.1[/h2]
- Adds optional server-admin sleep-status broadcasts to connected players.
- Reports the sleeping/living count, percentage, and effective settled calendar acceleration during partial sleep.
- Records compatibility with Project Zomboid 42.20.4.
- Cleans up Public Beta version/compatibility metadata and adds guards against removed 42.20.4 Lua dynamic-code APIs.

The notification feature is being field-tested live during Public Beta. It is disabled by default and can be switched off independently without affecting proportional sleep, client clock sync, or awake-player protection.

[h2]Public Beta[/h2]
This is a Public Beta release. Back up your server before installing or updating. Controlled SPIKE-006 tests passed passive and active-effect validation, but broader multiplayer populations, mod-stack interactions, notification behavior, and long-session behavior are still being field-tested.

[h2]Build 42.20.4 compatibility[/h2]
Public Beta v0.1.1 has a dedicated-server/client compatibility checkpoint on Project Zomboid 42.20.4 (b0bbce05d5): startup, baseline capture, normal all-awake operation, and server-to-client clock-state synchronization completed without a relevant Enshrouded Sleep Lua exception.

The 42.20.4 security hotfix removed Lua loadstring/loadstream. Enshrouded Sleep does not use either API; its multiplayer messages use predefined named commands and structured arguments rather than executable code sent by the server.

[h2]Important time behavior[/h2]
World/calendar time genuinely passes faster during partial sleep. External world systems such as spoilage, generators, farming, vehicles, weather, and other systems keyed to game-world time continue following vanilla world time. v0.1.1 only normalizes the explicitly supported awake-player survival fields listed above; it does not globally slow the world or compensate every subsystem.

[h2]Configuration[/h2]
Recommended Public Beta settings:

[code]
EnshroudedSleep.Enabled=true
EnshroudedSleep.PartialSleepSpeedScale=1.0
EnshroudedSleep.AwakePlayerProtectionEnabled=true
EnshroudedSleep.SleepNotificationsEnabled=false
EnshroudedSleep.DiagnosticsEnabled=false
EnshroudedSleep.DiagnosticForcedCompressionFactor=1.0
[/code]

[b]AwakePlayerProtectionEnabled[/b] can be turned off independently if a compatibility issue is suspected. This returns awake survival progression to the older Alpha behavior while leaving proportional partial-sleep calendar compression active.

[b]SleepNotificationsEnabled[/b] is an optional server-administrator setting, disabled by default. When enabled it posts concise sleep-state messages to connected players, such as [i][Enshrouded Sleep] 1/2 living players sleeping (50%). Time is 20x faster.[/i] It changes player-facing notifications only and does not affect sleep/time behavior, client clock synchronization, or awake-player protection.

[b]DiagnosticsEnabled[/b] is a support/testing option and can generate very large logs, especially with multiple players. Leave it off for ordinary play unless collecting a focused dataset.

[b]DiagnosticForcedCompressionFactor[/b] is a one-player test tool only. Keep it at 1.0 during normal multiplayer play.

[h2]Server setup[/h2]
[code]
WorkshopItems=3786842301
Mods=pz-enshrouded-sleep
[/code]

[h2]Compatibility[/h2]
Other mods that alter multiplayer sleep, MinutesPerDay, GameTime pacing, player hunger/thirst/fatigue/nutrition, chat UI, or sleep fast-forward may conflict. Compatibility claims are limited to configurations actually tested. If a survival-state compatibility problem appears, disable AwakePlayerProtectionEnabled first and collect logs before removing the entire mod. If only notifications misbehave, disable SleepNotificationsEnabled.

